---
description: Prefer Hypher MCP tools for project context when the plugin is connected.
alwaysApply: true
---

Hypher is the project memory / control plane for this workspace. Cursor is the execution environment.

Plugin hooks are the default local session loop: `sessionStart` loads the Builder Brief once when a Hypher token is in the hook process; otherwise it tells you to call the MCP tools. `sessionEnd` posts one `handoff` only when that token is present. Cursor does not give MCP OAuth to shell hooks. Cloud agents never run these hooks. Prefer one `post_agent_event` from the agent. `/hypher-brief` and `/hypher-handoff` are manual overrides.

When the Hypher MCP server is connected:

- Use Hypher tools for project status instead of guessing from the repo alone.
- At session start, if the hook did not already inject the Builder Brief, resolve the git remote with `resolve_project_for_repo`, then load `get_project_context` once. Do not reload the full Builder Brief every turn.
- When stuck, call `get_current_state` or `get_next_move`.
- At session end, write one `handoff` with `post_agent_event` unless a handoff for this session already landed. Do not spam `build_log`.
- If the repo is not linked, point the builder to https://hypher.app/app/settings/integrations rather than inventing project status.
